AB  - Reliable and accurate prediction of precipitation is of great practical value. Focusing on the post-processing of ensemble precipitation forecasts from numerical weather prediction (NWP) models, this paper introduces Pyenspp—a Python package that integrates preprocessing, calibration, dependence reconstruction, and verification into a unified workflow. Specifically, the package enables extraction of area-weighted precipitation forecasts, supports three transformation methods to mitigate precipitation skewness, and implements ensemble calibration using both quantile mapping (QM) and the proposed Kolmogorov–Arnold Network–Censored Shifted Gamma Distribution (KAN–CSGD) model. The Schaake Shuffle (SS) is incorporated to restore temporal coherence across lead times, and comprehensive verification metrics are provided. Case study results demonstrate that KAN–CSGD effectively reduces bias and improves forecast reliability compared to raw forecasts, outperforming QM. The SS further enhances forecast skill for accumulated precipitation across lead times. Pyenspp offers a practical, extensible tool for environmental prediction and management.
ER  - 
